# AutoTuneX — BASH runner example configuration (granite.build, standalone)
#
# Runner: the granite.build "bash" launcher (AUTOTUNEX_JOB_BACKEND=llmb together
# with GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone). Emits the space://environments/bash +
# space://steps/autotune build.yaml and submits it through the llmb CLI. It
# demonstrates granite.build ⇄ AutoTuneX integration on a laptop/Mac (MPS/CPU
# via mlx).
#
# Use it:
#   export GB_TOKEN=<your gb token>     # REQUIRED — see the note below
#   cp envs/bash.env.example .env
#   make dev
#
# GB_TOKEN must be EXPORTED into the shell, not merely written here: the
# reconcile loop authenticates to gbserver with it over HTTP, and startup
# refuses to run if the variable is absent (its value is never read into
# Settings).
#
# Runtime prerequisite: `llmb artifact push` is disabled in standalone mode, so
# datasets are stored LOCALLY here, not HuggingFace-hosted — see the dataset
# storage note below.
#
# This file covers what the bash runner needs for development. For everything
# else — the optional auth providers (OIDC / BFF / API keys), serving the built
# UI, dataset-preview tuning, and the LLM-intelligence feature — see the full
# menu in the root .env.example. Every AUTOTUNEX_ variable is documented in
# src/autotunex/core/config.py.
# Runner design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-11-local-and-bash-runners-design.md

# --- Application -----------------------------------------------------------
AUTOTUNEX_APP_NAME="AutoTuneX API"
# dev | test | prod
AUTOTUNEX_ENVIRONMENT=dev
AUTOTUNEX_DEBUG=false
AUTOTUNEX_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
AUTOTUNEX_API_PREFIX=/api/v1

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite for local development; no server needed.
AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:///./autotunex.db
AUTOTUNEX_DATABASE_ECHO=false
# Create missing tables on startup (dev convenience; use `make migrate` in prod).
AUTOTUNEX_AUTO_CREATE_SCHEMA=true

# --- Artifact storage ------------------------------------------------------
AUTOTUNEX_ARTIFACT_DIR=./artifacts

# --- Auth (standalone / dev) -----------------------------------------------
# A JSON array, NOT a comma-separated list. "disabled" is standalone mode: every
# caller is the same principal. Leaving STANDALONE_EMAIL unset attributes writes
# to a default system owner (standalone@autotunex.local).
AUTOTUNEX_AUTH_PROVIDERS=["disabled"]
# AUTOTUNEX_STANDALONE_EMAIL=you@example.com
AUTOTUNEX_STANDALONE_ROLE=admin
# AUTOTUNEX_AUTO_PROVISION_USERS=true

# --- Execution: the bash launcher (granite.build standalone) ---------------
# JOB_BACKEND=llmb selects the llmb launcher; GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone makes it
# emit the local-bash spec instead of the remote custom_code spec.
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_BACKEND=llmb
# NOTE: GB_ENVIRONMENT is granite.build's own variable and is UNPREFIXED (no
# AUTOTUNEX_). "standalone" selects the bash spec.
GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone

# Base URL of the local gbserver the reconcile loop polls for job status.
# REQUIRED for the llmb backend — without it an accepted job sits "pending"
# forever (the reconcile loop is the only thing that advances it).
AUTOTUNEX_GB_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:9000

# Name of the env var holding the gb auth token (see the export note above).
AUTOTUNEX_GB_TOKEN_ENV=GB_TOKEN

# The llmb CLI binary name or path used to submit builds.
AUTOTUNEX_LLMB_COMMAND=llmb

# Values embedded in the local-bash build's bash.env. FM_TUNE_ROOT is the
# fm-tune checkout *or* repo. With fm-tune vendored in-tree, point it at the
# local checkout and leave FM_TUNE_REF unset — the tree is already at the
# right commit:
#   AUTOTUNEX_BASH_FM_TUNE_ROOT=/abs/path/to/granite.build/autotunex/src/fm-tune
# Otherwise FM_TUNE_ROOT takes a repo URL and FM_TUNE_REF optionally pins a
# branch/tag/commit (unset uses the repo's default branch). BACKEND is "mlx"
# (Apple Silicon) or "torch".
# AUTOTUNEX_BASH_FM_TUNE_ROOT=https://github.example.com/org/fm-tune
# AUTOTUNEX_BASH_FM_TUNE_REF=main
AUTOTUNEX_BASH_FM_TUNE_EXTRA=full,mlx
AUTOTUNEX_BASH_BACKEND=mlx

# Where the generated build.yaml is written (<dir>/<job_id>/build.yaml).
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_SPEC_DIR=tmp

# The api-bridge / callback base URL the build reports to (optional; the
# local-bash build ALWAYS emits it as AUTOTUNEX_SERVER_URL, defaulting to
# http://localhost:8001 — the api-bridge — when unset).
# AUTOTUNEX_JOB_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:8001

# How often the reconcile loop sweeps non-terminal jobs, and the per-sweep read cap.
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECONDS=30
AUTOTUNEX_JOB_RECONCILE_CONCURRENCY=5

# --- Dataset storage (local backend) ----------------------------------------
# This is the same-host bash runner: `llmb artifact push` is disabled under
# GB_ENVIRONMENT=standalone, so "huggingface" is not usable here — forcing it
# fails startup. "auto" (the default) resolves to LOCAL storage instead and
# emits an absolute file:// locator that gbserver mounts as the build's
# dataset_files input, so no HF token is needed for datasets on this runner.
AUTOTUNEX_DATASET_STORAGE_BACKEND=auto
# Optional HF org/namespace prefix for the pushed dataset repo (non-standalone only).
# AUTOTUNEX_HF_NAMESPACE=your-org
